  "id": "beiguan",
  "name": "Beiguan (Taiwanese temple ensemble and luantan theatre)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Loud ensemble and theatre music of Taiwan's Hoklo communities, also called luantan, transmitted by amateur clubs attached to temples, notably in Yilan and Changhua, and heard at temple festivals, processions and funerals. Its paizi suites set paired suona over drum, gongs and cymbals, while its theatre arias, sung in stylized guanhua, are accompanied by hard-bowed fiddles led by the coconut-shell kezaixian; clubs are divided between the rival xipi and fulu schools.",
  "recipe": "classic modern beiguan, carnival Processional, east Asian branch. suona, cutting coconut shell bright piercing kezaixian, danpigu, gong tamtam, naobo. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
